reets that blend Georgian elegance with the Mediterranean soul.<\/span><\/p><p><strong><span class=\"gmail-selected\">What will you discover on this tour?<\/span><\/strong><\/p><ul><li><p><span class=\"gmail-selected\">The <\/span><strong><span class=\"gmail-selected\">Pla\u00e7a de s\u2019Esplanada<\/span><\/strong><span class=\"gmail-selected\">, the social heart of the city.<\/span><\/p><\/li><li><p><span class=\"gmail-selected\">The unique architecture of its <\/span><strong><span class=\"gmail-selected\">Georgian-style buildings<\/span><\/strong><span class=\"gmail-selected\">, a legacy of the 18th century.<\/span><\/p><\/li><li><p><span class=\"gmail-selected\">The <\/span><strong><span class=\"gmail-selected\">Teatro Principal de Mah\u00f3n<\/span><\/strong><span class=\"gmail-selected\">, one of the oldest opera houses in Spain.<\/span><\/p><\/li><li><p><span class=\"gmail-selected\">The historic <\/span><strong><span class=\"gmail-selected\">Mercado del Claustro del Carmen<\/span><\/strong><span class=\"gmail-selected\">, full of life and local products.<\/span><\/p><\/li><li><p><span class=\"gmail-selected\">The Town Hall (Sa Sala) and the <\/span><strong><span class=\"gmail-selected\">Church of Santa Mar\u00eda<\/span><\/strong><span class=\"gmail-selected\">, with its imposing facade.<\/span><\/p><\/li><li><p><span class=\"gmail-selected\">Strategic viewpoints with spectacular views of the port.<\/span><\/p><\/li><\/ul><p><strong><span class=\"gmail-selected\">Languages:<\/span><\/strong><span class=\"gmail-selected\"> Spanish, English, and French. <\/span><strong><span class=\"gmail-selected\">Duration:<\/span><\/strong><span class=\"gmail-selected\"> 2 hours.<\/span><\/p><p><strong><span class=\"gmail-selected\">Includes:<\/span><\/strong><\/p><ul><li><p><span class=\"gmail-selected\">Walking tour with an accredited official guide.<\/span><\/p><\/li><li><p><span class=\"gmail-selected\">Detailed historical and cultural explanations.<\/span><\/p><\/li><